From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps open files with ChromeOS's default apps

Linux apps open links and files through nickel-open (the handler of
org.nickelos.ChromeOS.desktop, which xdg-open, GIO and the OpenURI portal
use on NickelOS). Links go to Ash's UrlHandlerService; for files this adds
VmApplicationsService.NickelOpenPath(path, how): ChromeOS opens the file
with the app it opens that kind of file with, the user's default (as the
Files app does), opens a folder in Files ("folder"), or shows a file in its
folder ("show"). Paths in /home/chronos/user, Linux apps' home, are taken
as the profile directory it mounts, where ChromeOS's volumes are. Failures
show ChromeOS's own notification. So one set of defaults (Files, Settings >
Apps > Default apps) applies to every app.

